## Original Content
Ils conseillent depuis des années les formations de gauche en Europe et aux États-Unis. Leur idée fixe : instaurer une taxe sur le patrimoine des plus riches. À court terme, leurs espoirs portent sur la Californie et la France.

## Summary
Economists Gabriel Zucman, Thomas Piketty, and Emmanuel Saez have advised left-wing parties in Europe and the US for years, focusing on implementing a wealth tax on the richest individuals. Their immediate efforts target California and France for policy adoption. The article highlights their ideological influence on political strategies.

## Key Points
- Gabriel Zucman, Thomas Piketty, and Emmanuel Saez are economists advising left-wing parties on economic policies.
- Their central goal is to establish a wealth tax targeting the richest individuals.
- Current short-term hopes for implementing this tax are focused on California and France.
- They have a long-standing role in shaping economic discourse for parties like PS and LFI.


